The posterior mean of μ is 0.0011, and its 95% credible interval (0.0005, 0.0017) excludes zero, which indicates a small positive typical daily return over the sample period. The scale parameter 
σ has posterior mean 0.0063 (95% CI 0.0058 to 0.0069). 
The posterior mean of ν is 3.81 with a 95% credible interval of (2.86, 5.04).This indicates that VOO returns have much heavier tails than a Normal distribution.Because the interval includes values below 4, the fourth moment of the fitted model may not exist, so we interpret tail heaviness through ν and not through model kurtosis.

##Model Fit

Figure 4 shows the QQ-plot against the fitted Student-t, using the posterior estimates. The points lie close to the 45-degree line, including in the tails, which is clearly better than the Normal QQ-plot in Figure 2. So the Student-t is a better description of the unconditional distribution of VOO returns. 

